            <div xml:id="d131">

                <pb facs="0299" n="185" sameAs="frus:frus1931v01/pg185"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">462.00R296/4480: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Belgium</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Gibson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Acting Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Brussels</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-07-14T00:00:00+01:00">July 14,
                        1931—midnight</date>.<lb/>[Received July 15—5:16 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>84. Reference is made to my telegram No. 82, July 14, 6 p.m. The Belgian
                    Government is now working out a formula for notification to the B. I. S. of
                    provisional postponement of German payments tomorrow.</p>
                <pb facs="0300" n="186" xml:id="pg186"/>
                <p>The Belgian Government has formally accepted the British invitation to the London
                    Conference and is sending a delegation tomorrow.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gibson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
